+fix = "the turns file delivers its chunks with no delay and holds the finish (`hangMs`), and a snap that shows streamed lines waits out both pacers, so a snap or a keystroke mid-turn meets the same text on both; or a capture.sh `waitfor <text>` verb (not a scenario file). Applied to interrupt (interrupt-words.json) and interrupt2 (interrupt-lines.json, its mid snap at 6 s): two retakes each give the same verdicts. Not applied to interrupt-steer, provider, rename-midturn, resume-empty (slow-line-turn.json), which time a keystroke against the stream on purpose and need their own check"
+why = "The fake gateway streams a chunk every `delayMs`; a snap or an Escape at a fixed second lands at a different chunk on each binary (`↑4 ↓31` / `↑4 ↓43`, line 18 or 17 at the cancel, word 13 or 11 at the steer)."
